<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5410" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμολγός</span></b> , ὁ, <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i> always in the phrase <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νυκτὸς
		ἀμολγῷ,</span> usu. of <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>dead</i> of night, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				11.173
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				15.324
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Merc.</u>
				7
			</span></i>; also of evening twilight, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				22.317
			</span></i> (when Venus is seen), and morning twilight, ib.<i><span class="en">
				28
			</span></i> (when Sirius rises in autumn); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱερᾶς νυκτὸς ἀμολγόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					69
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμολγός</span> alone, <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>H.</u>
				34.12
			</span></i>, f.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				781.6
			</span></i>:—as Adj., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νύξ</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				104
			</span></i>. (Derived by <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1018.21
			</span></i> from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμολγός,</span> Achaean for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκμή,</span> but more prob. =
			<i>milking-time.</i>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
